Bundled font assets
===================

All three font files are used by the drawcustom renderer and are bundled
so that drawing a label never needs the network. Regenerate them with
scripts/fetch_assets.py.


Roboto-Regular.ttf, Roboto-Bold.ttf
-----------------------------------

Roboto, from

    https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Unmodified. This is the default text font. Pillow's own built in font
covers ASCII only - it draws "Müller" as a box where the umlaut belongs -
which rules it out for anything but English. Roboto is also what the
ESPHome Designer previews a layout with, so a design carries over.


materialdesignicons-webfont.ttf, mdi-codepoints.json
----------------------------------------------------

Material Design Icons, version 7.4.47, from

    https://github.com/Templarian/MaterialDesign-Webfont

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as above.

The font file is unmodified. mdi-codepoints.json is generated from that
project's scss/_variables.scss; it holds nothing but the icon names and
the glyph positions they live at, which is what lets an "icon" element in
a payload be written as "mdi:battery-50".
